    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW23izoKDnQGmGSyNawiWw51j)_\n\n## Problem\n- `sp-academic` failed to load with `Key sequence C-c w b b starts with non-prefix key C-c w b`, and `bibtex` and `citar` failed with the same cause.\n- Cause: `sp-collection-query-tables` (from #329) bound `C-c w b` as a command (`sp-collec-query-book-open`). `C-c w b` is the Bibliographic prefix (`C-c w b b/r/o/c/...`), so every longer sequence was refused.\n\n## Change\n- Rebind the book table command to `C-c w B` (free; sits next to `C-c w T`/`V`).\n- Updated the `.el` and the literate doc (key table, binding block, command text, changelog line).\n- GUI-only, no CUA-conflicting keys; no other binding touched.\n\n## Not tested\n- Not loaded in a real Emacs here; the change is a one-key rebind, and no other `C-c w B` binding exists in the config.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiChyWCx6usJhYBdwzr)_",
